ople denying Humanity to a  large number of people they they would  seem to be much much more radical and so  a question then becomes what what are  people going to say about us you know  there is there is no neutrality there's  no middle ground here between do we kill  850 000 babies a year or do we not kill  I guess the middle ground is we kill 400  000 babies a year but that's not much of  a middle ground you know King Solomon  talked about this too uh so uh you know  which side are you going to be on if you  throw your hands up in the air you  you've made a decision if you just sort  of allow this sort of thing to happen  without any pushback at all you you have  absolutely made made a decision can I  ask for well I want to ask two things  before I let you go one  and I asked you this a little bit  earlier but we got off track how did you  learn to climb I mean how did you start  you know you're pretty young man right  now when did this start yeah this  started in high school I uh grew up in  Michigan hunting and fishing and you  know I was outside every day and then uh  my dad he was a carpenter and it just  got hard on his body doing construction  so we moved to LA and California the  hunting's just so much different than  Michigan so I needed something else  outdoorsy to do so uh my dad he he  bought me a rope some quick draws and a  harness and I learned how to rock climb  off of YouTube and we would go out on  the weekends maybe once a month and go  rock climbing but when I graduated high  school I actually skipped my graduation  and I moved to Yosemite and that was  where you know Yosemite Valley is just  the gauntlet it is the mecca of rock  climbing so that's where I really got my  feet wet and uh you know  it's so crazy I never thought I'd be  climbing skyscrapers uh or like the  other day someone approached me and they  want to make a comic book out of me and  I'm like I never in my life did I ever  think I would have my own comic book but  here I am and I'm so grateful that  everyone is supporting me and and uh you  know donating money to let them live.org  I think it's just absolutely fabulous a  total inspiration everybody should go  check out  letthelive.org everybody should keep up  with Mason's work obviously and I want  the comic book when can I go buy this  comic book  you know it's a work in progress It's a  hard thing to make a comic book about  abortion so we're trying to work out a  way to do it  we're maybe going for Johnny The Walrus  yeah kind of kind of angle you know like  like make it about abortion but not yeah  with a lighter touch but I I agree that  it is tough it is tough to make a  cartoon or or a a comic book about it  but listen you've done harder things  okay you've climbed a thousand foot  building all right so so uh I I have no  doubt that it will happen Mason  incredible work really keep it up just  so inspirational and everybody go keep  up with Mason descham the pro-life  Spider-Man thank you Michael  foreign  [Music]  [Music]
 

